===[[Marvel Comics|Marvel]]===
The Marvel Comics series ''[[Godzilla (Marvel comic)|Godzilla]]'' told original stories and attempted to both fit into the official Toho continuity and avoid referencing it too directly. It also integrated Godzilla into the Marvel Universe, making use of many of its main regular characters, such as the Avengers and the Fantastic Four.
====''[[Godzilla (Marvel comic)|Godzilla]]'' to [[Mighty Avengers issue 1|''Mighty Avengers'' #1]]====
[[File:Marvel_Godzilla_Full.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Godzilla in Marvel's ''[[Godzilla (Marvel comic)|Godzilla]]'']]
{{Main|Godzilla (Marvel Earth-616)}}
[[Godzilla (Marvel Earth-616)|Marvel's Godzilla]] was first awakened in 1956 after an underwater H-bomb test. For 20 years, he both terrorized Japan and protected it from other monsters before disappearing. He reappeared in Alaska in the late 1970s and soon traveled down to the U.S. mainland. S.H.I.E.L.D. tried to stop him several times, but failed. He fought other monsters and superhero teams during his journey across the country, even foiling an alien invasion. He was shrunken down in size and sent back to the Cretaceous Period through a time machine, but soon appeared in New York again at his full size. He fought the Fantastic Four and the Avengers along with S.H.I.E.L.D., but was eventually turned away by a young Japanese boy named Robert "Little Rob" Takaguchi. He swam out into the Atlantic Ocean.

Years later, Godzilla was captured and mutated by [[Douglas Birley|Doctor Demonicus]], turning him into a more water-based reptile. He no longer had his atomic breath and was mind-controlled by the mad doctor. He later attacked the Avengers, but the pilot, Tigra, escaped. He was stopped from attacking a village and was taken out to sea by Iron Man. Iron Man took off his armor and Godzilla took it back to Demonicus. He later escaped into the ocean, found the set of ''Devil Dinosaur: The Movie'', and was attacked by a robotic {{Plain link|[https://marvel.wikia.com/wiki/Devil_Dinosaur_(Earth-78411) Devil Dinosaur]}}. He fought and destroyed it and returned to the sea. After an unknown amount of time, Godzilla returned to his original form and attacked New York under the control of the Mole Man. Godzilla has not been seen since then, though other Godzilla-like creatures have occasionally been sighted. 
