===[[IDW Publishing|IDW]]===
[[IDW Publishing]] has released several Godzilla comic book series. The three main series, ''[[Godzilla: Kingdom of Monsters]]'', ''[[Godzilla (2012 comic)|Godzilla]]'' and ''[[Godzilla: Rulers of Earth]]'', are part of a single ongoing storyline, while the various miniseries are each self-contained stories.
====''[[Godzilla: Kingdom of Monsters]]''====
[[File:Godzilla GKoM.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Godzilla in ''[[Godzilla: Kingdom of Monsters]]'']]
Godzilla awakened one day from underneath a beach near Japan. The military attempted to kill Godzilla with an atomic bomb, but it only made him more powerful and granted him the ability to fire atomic breath. Elsewhere around the world, the monsters [[Rodan]], [[Anguirus]], [[Kumonga]] and [[Battra]] appeared and began to wreak havoc. Eventually, all of the monsters converged on the [[United States]] and battled each other, causing untold destruction. The U.S. government built a giant robot, [[Mechagodzilla]], in order to battle the monsters while in Asia, a monk awakened [[King Ghidorah]] to battle them. Godzilla arrived in Washington D.C., where he was attacked by King Ghidorah. Mechagodzilla, piloted by [[Steven Woods]], arrived and defeated both monsters, earning Woods a hero's recognition. Meanwhile, the evil psychic twins [[Minette and Mallory]] took control of Rodan and Battra and came to the U.S. to try and control Godzilla. Godzilla managed to overcome and defeat both monsters and later returned to the sea, leaving human civilization devastated and rushing to prepare for future monster attacks.
{{Clear}}
====''[[Godzilla: Gangsters & Goliaths]]''====
[[File:Godzilla G&G.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Godzilla in ''[[Godzilla: Gangsters & Goliaths]]'']]
{{Main|Godzilla (Godzilla: Gangsters & Goliaths)}}
Godzilla was living on [[Monster Island]] along with most of the other kaiju on Earth. When [[Tokyo]] police detective Makoto Sato brought the [[Shobijin|Elias]] to Tokyo, Godzilla and the other monsters came ashore and laid waste to the city. Sato's son, a pilot in [[G-Force]], took command of [[Mechagodzilla]] and used it to fight Godzilla while Sato brought down the evil Yakuza boss Ryota Takahashi and returned the Elias to [[Mothra]]. After the Elias were safely returned, Godzilla and the other monsters returned to Monster Island in peace.
{{Clear}}
====''[[Godzilla Legends]]''====
[[File:Godzilla (Legends).jpg|thumb|right|200px|Godzilla in ''[[Godzilla Legends]]'' [[Godzilla Legends issue 1|#1]]]]
====="[[Godzilla Legends issue 1|The Underdog]]"=====
Dr. [[Brian Anders]] recounted how his research, intended to attract whales, instead drew Godzilla, also known as Kaiju Alpha, who sank his ship and attacked a nearby city. Anders also mentioned that [[Anguirus]]' first appearance involved a battle with Godzilla and that [[Destoroyah]] was the most powerful monster humanity had encountered other than Godzilla. After Anguirus defeated Destoroyah with the assistance of the Kaiju Defense Force, he returned to the ocean only for Godzilla to surfaced in front of him. Godzilla did not attack him but merely stared at him briefly; while Major [[Samantha Tagger]] theorized Godzilla now viewed Anguirus with respect, Anders instead thought that Godzilla simply didn't see Anguirus as a threat and was vindicated when Godzilla chose to attack the Kaiju Defense Force aircraft carrier.
====="[[Godzilla Legends issue 3|Secrets]]"=====
During Institute orientation, Godzilla briefly appeared onscreen as headmaster [[Mugal]] described the kaiju epidemic and how [[Miki Saegusa]] was able to avert disaster using her telepathic connection to Godzilla.
====="[[Godzilla Legends issue 4|Smog of War]]"=====
[[Mechagodzilla]] landed in the destroyed city of Linfen, [[China]] after a monster presumed to be Godzilla attacked it. The crew searched for Godzilla but were surprised at the lack of radiological presence as toxicity levels rose and [[Hedorah]] attacked them and then flew away. As Hedorah flew through the air, Godzilla's atomic breath suddenly shot out of the sea and hit Hedorah, sending it crashing down nearby. Mechagodzilla fired on Godzilla but Godzilla ignored Mechagodzilla and engaged Hedorah, corroding his hand upon contact with Hedorah but having some success with his atomic breath. Mechagodzilla then fired its Mega Buster at both of them but was knocked aside as Hedorah began to smother Godzilla. Mechagodzilla fired its plasma grenade at both monsters, but to little effect, as Hedorah continued smothering Godzilla despite Godzilla ripping out two yellow orbs from Hedorah's body. Mechagodzilla's crew ultimately decided to go against their orders and fired Shock Anchors into Hedorah, electrocuting it and making it turn its attention to Mechagodzilla as the machine flew into the atmosphere while holding Hedorah. Godzilla recovered and returned to the sea as Mechagodzilla seemingly destroyed the frozen Hedorah with its plasma grenade, unaware of four surviving Hedorah tadpoles.
====="[[Godzilla Legends issue 5|From a Great Height]]"=====
Famous thrillseeker [[Bryson Allworth]] was approached after 15 years of retirement by his government and tasked with climbing Godzilla to collect tissue samples to further research on the monster. Clad in a special radiation suit, he successfully jumped onto Godzilla as his jeep drove past his tail and began to climb the monster as he traveled through rural Mongolia. Allworth collected tissue samples from Godzilla's dorsal fins and discovered a "[[List of minor Toho monsters#Irradiated Bird|weird new species of bird]]" which had made a nest on Godzilla's back. Unfortunately for Allworth, it began to rain, complicated his climb. Allworth was also horrified when Godzilla rampaged through a village, not even noticing a tear in his suit as he was rattled by the destruction left on the kaiju's wake. Allworth had almost made it to the top at this point, but had to retreat into Godzilla's dorsal fins as he fell into one of [[Kumonga]]'s quicksand traps and the two did battle. Godzilla was webbed up by Kumonga but destroyed it with a nuclear pulse Allworth miraculously survived. Godzilla then blasted Kumonga with atomic breath and beat the spider into retreat with its own torn-off leg, finishing it off with a tail-whip. Godzilla then walked away as Allworth was picked up by a helicopter Godzilla nearly destroyed with atomic breath.

Allworth revealed all this in an interview, as well as the cancer he suffered from as a result of radiation entering the tear in his suit. He did not hate Godzilla, however, and called for more understanding of the monster, justifying this by explaining Godzilla was simply another living being who wanted to live his life in peace. Allworth was, however, interrupted by the announcement that Godzilla was attacking Melbourne, and he lamented the rash response to this news by the interviewer and staff.
{{Clear}}

====''[[Godzilla (2012 comic)|Godzilla]]''====
[[File:Godzilla (Ongoing).jpg|thumb|right|200px|Godzilla in ''[[Godzilla (2012 comic)|Godzilla]]'']]
In this follow-up to ''[[Godzilla: Kingdom of Monsters]]'', Godzilla appeared in Washington D.C. once again, where the ex-British Special Forces agent known as Boxer, whose daughter was killed by Godzilla, was hired to protect a wealthy Japanese businesswoman's daughter. Boxer's client was killed during their attempted escape, so Boxer decided to join with his former acquaintances to form the "Kaiju Kill Crew," a group of mercenaries hired to bring down attacking kaiju. After several successful missions, Boxer's crew was sent to California, where a billionaire industrialist had just unleashed his new [[Mechagodzilla]] to battle Godzilla. After Godzilla defeated Mechagodzilla, Boxer and his team tried to bring Godzilla down as he headed north along the Pacific Coast to Seattle. But when the space monsters [[Hedorah]], [[Gigan]], [[SpaceGodzilla]] and [[Monster X]] arrived on Earth, Boxer was forced to temporary abandon his vendetta against Godzilla to defeat the space monsters. While Mechagodzilla freed the monsters held on [[Monster Island]], Godzilla battled and defeated Hedorah in California, then traveled to [[New York]] to take on SpaceGodzilla and Monster X. There, he was joined by Mechagodzilla and Kumonga, who were both promptly defeated. But when the immobilized Mechagodzilla froze SpaceGodzilla with the Absolute Zero Cannon, Godzilla took the opportunity to defeat his extraterrestrial clone with a blast of his atomic breath. With only him and Godzilla still standing, Monster X transformed into Keizer Ghidorah and quickly overwhelmed Godzilla. Thankfully, [[Rodan]] arrived and decapitated one of Keizer Ghidorah's heads with a sonic boom from his wings. With Rodan's help, Godzilla severed another one of Keizer Ghidorah's heads, then killed him by crushing his remaining head with his foot. As Godzilla started walking back to the ocean, Boxer jumped into Godzilla's mouth in a last-ditch attempt to hurt him using a miniature version of his "headache gun." This action only slightly irritated Godzilla, at the cost of Boxer's life.
====''[[Godzilla: The Half-Century War]]'' and "[[Godzilla: 70th Anniversary|The Half-Century Bore]]"====
[[File:Godzilla THCW.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Godzilla in ''[[Godzilla: The Half-Century War]]'']]
Godzilla suddenly appeared in [[Tokyo]] in [[1954]], setting the entire city ablaze. Ota Murakami and his friend Kentaro Yoshihara were sent in as part of a [[JSDF]] platoon to deal with the crisis. The two managed to save countless civilians from Godzilla, and barely escaped the disaster area with their lives. A few days later, a special [[Oxygen Destroyer|chemical weapon]] was detonated in [[Tokyo Bay]] and seemingly killed Godzilla; however, Godzilla was soon spotted elsewhere in the [[Pacific Ocean]] and Ota and Kentaro were recruited into the Anti-Megalosaurus Force (AMF), a special international military force dedicated to hunting giant monsters. In [[1967]], Godzilla was sighted in Vietnam during the height of the Vietnam War. The AMF deployed a unit of [[Maser Cannon]]s to battle the creature, but their assault was interrupted by the appearance of another monster, [[Anguirus]]. Godzilla and Anguirus battled each other until Anguirus found himself overwhelmed and decided to flee. As the Maser Tanks prepared to fire at Godzilla, their view was obscured by the smoke from a bombing run and Godzilla escaped. In both [[1971]] and [[1974]], Godzilla clashed with [[Hedorah]] in Istanbul, [[Turkey]]. In [[1975]], Godzilla, [[Rodan]], [[Mothra]], [[Battra]], Hedorah, [[Ebirah]], [[Megalon]] and [[Kumonga]] appeared in Ghana, prompting various elite AMF teams to respond. There, Ota discovered that Dr. Deverich, a former AMF scientist, had stolen an experimental device and weaponized it to attract monsters, intending to sell it to the criminal underworld. During the chaos, Deverich attracted all of the monsters to his location, allowing him to escape while the monsters overran the AMF's forces. The AMF's commander, Colonel Schooler, was killed in the attack, only strengthening Ota's hatred of Godzilla. In [[1987]], Godzilla appeared in Bombay, drawn there by Deverich's transmitter. Ota and Kentaro traveled there to hunt down Deverich while the AMF deployed their latest weapon, [[Mechagodzilla]]. Ota and Kentaro apprehended Deverich, but not before he activated his new more powerful monster transmitter, which summoned [[SpaceGodzilla]] to the city. SpaceGodzilla severely damaged Mechagodzilla and began to overpower Godzilla. Ota took command of the damaged Mechagodzilla and used it to destroy the giant crystals giving SpaceGodzilla his power, toppling it onto him. Godzilla used this opportunity to blast SpaceGodzilla with his atomic breath, killing him. In [[2002]], the AMF had developed two new anti-Godzilla weapons; a new Mechagodzilla and the [[Dimension Tide]], an artificial black hole gun. Godzilla was lured to [[Antarctica]], but the space monsters [[King Ghidorah]] and [[Gigan]], who had been drawn to Earth by Deverich's transmitter years ago, arrived there as well. While the Dimension Tide prepared to fire, Ota wished Kentaro farewell and took command of Mechagodzilla, assisting Godzilla in battling the space monsters. After the Dimension Tide was fired, Mechagodzilla and Godzilla ensured that both space monsters were banished into the resulting black hole. Before Godzilla could leave, Ota restrained Godzilla with Mechagodzilla and yelled at him, telling him to look at him. As Mechagodzilla was torn apart by the force of the black hole, the cockpit was exposed, allowing Ota to briefly make eye contact with Godzilla. Mechagodzilla then released Godzilla, causing both monsters to apparently be pulled into the black hole; however, Godzilla somehow escaped and swam away after the black hole dissipated, unseen by anyone.

====''[[Godzilla: Rulers of Earth]]''====
Godzilla from ''Godzilla: Kingdom of Monsters'' and ''Godzilla'' returns once again in ''[[Godzilla: Rulers of Earth]]''.
====''[[Godzilla: Cataclysm]]''====
[[File:Godzilla_Cataclysm_Issue_1_-_Godzilla.png|thumb|right|200px|Godzilla in [[Godzilla: Cataclysm issue 1|''Godzilla: Cataclysm'' #1]]]]
{{Main|Godzilla (Godzilla: Cataclysm)}}
Godzilla had been a menace to [[human]]ity for many years, but was enraged alongside the other monsters by humanity's attempt to mind-control them, leading to an apocalyptic war which wiped out most of the human race. Godzilla suddenly reappeared after 20 years to fight the plant monster [[Biollante]] in the ruins of [[Tokyo]], unwilling to allow her to restore [[Earth]]'s greenery and potentially let humanity recover. Despite Mothra also reappearing to protect Biollante from Godzilla's wrath, the pair were unsuccessful at stopping him, as Biollante was reduced to just her core and Mothra was forced to retreat. After the human survivor [[Shiori]] recovered the core and it began to rapidly [[Regeneration|regenerate]], it attracted the attention of [[Megaguirus]] and her [[Meganulon|Meganula]] swarm. Their battle with Mothra was interrupted by Godzilla, who shot Megaguirus out of the sky with his atomic breath. As Godzilla defeated Mothra next, the demon [[Destoroyah]] rose from the sea with the intention of killing everything. Godzilla appeared to battle Destoroyah and struggled against the horror until both Mothra and the regenerating Biollante intervened on his behalf, allowing him to kill Destoroyah with a blast of his spiral heat ray. Godzilla then chose to leave humanity and Biollante in peace, returning to the ocean.
{{Clear}}
====''[[Godzilla in Hell]]''====
[[File:Egglezilla.png|thumb|right|200px|Godzilla in [[Godzilla in Hell issue 2|''Godzilla in Hell'' #2]]]]
{{Main|Godzilla (Godzilla in Hell)}}
Following a fateful battle against [[SpaceGodzilla]] that killed them both and obliterated [[Earth]], Godzilla found himself in a celestial realm. He rejected the [[God-mountain]]'s demands to join the angels there in their war against [[Underworld|Hell]] and was promptly banished to that lower realm. He triumphed over a revived SpaceGodzilla with angelic assistance, but again dismissed an alliance with the God-mountain and descended deeper into Hell, determined to return to the living world. He faced numerous adversaries during his journey, including a [[Doppelganger demon|demon]] which initially took on his appearance; demonic versions of [[Demon Rodan|Rodan]], [[Demon Anguirus|Anguirus]], and [[Demon Varan|Varan]]; [[King Ghidorah]]; devilish versions of [[Devilish King Ghidorah|King Ghidorah]] and [[Devilish Destoroyah|Destoroyah]]; and a [[God-demon]] guarding an exit from Hell. He only triumphed over this last foe when a swarm of [[Hellbat]]s ate him alive, allowing him to possess them and reform after unleashing a final attack. Exiting Hell, he found himself in an ocean and roared in victory.
{{Clear}}
====''[[Godzilla: Oblivion]]''====
[[File:Godzilla_in_Godzilla_Oblivion.jpg|thumb|right|200px|Godzilla in [[Godzilla: Oblivion issue 2|''Godzilla: Oblivion'' #2]]]]
{{Main|Godzilla (Godzilla: Oblivion)}}
Following an apocalyptic event in "Earth-2" in which kaiju brought an end to human civilization, Godzilla established himself as the strongest monster and the world's ecological ruler, forcing the remaining humans to try to work with him and keep him happy. Ten years later, scientists from an alternate dimension with no monsters which later called itself "Earth-1" were able to make a portal between dimensions and visited "Earth-2", encountering the world's people and Godzilla after an incident with a small [[Rodan]]. After [[King Ghidorah]] entered the portal and attacked "Earth-1", a world unused to monsters, plans were made to lure King Ghidorah back to "Earth-2" but the plan was changed when they arrived to bring Godzilla to "Earth-1" and have him fight King Ghidorah, with the plan being successfully carried out as Godzilla reunited with King Ghidorah on the other side of the portal. The two immediately began to fight as Godzilla blasted his foe with atomic breath only for King Ghidorah to use gravity beams in response. Their fight continued until King Ghidorah picked Godzilla up and flew him over the ocean only for a barrage of nuclear missiles to engulf both monsters with the result of Godzilla being unharmed but King Ghidorah killed and his middle head missing. Running increasingly low on options, an army of [[Mechagodzilla]]s was sent to engage him as King Ghidorah was revived as [[Mecha-King Ghidorah]]. Godzilla destroyed the Mechagodzillas and attacked the hangar holding Mecha-King Ghidorah just as the cyborg was completed. As the two began to fight, the inhabitants of "Earth-2" reopened the portal and sent the rest of their monsters through, having matured to full size in Godzilla's absence. As Godzilla and Mecha-King Ghidorah found themselves surrounded, they faced off against each other and various other monsters, with Godzilla battling the imago Mothra and a mature Rodan as Mecha-King Ghidorah fought the entire Mothra family and [[Anguirus]]. During the chaos, numerous portals were activated across "Earth-1" to allow people to escape as Godzilla defeated both Mecha-King Ghidorah and [[Hedorah]]. Godzilla then spotted Dr. [[Eli Talbert]] and Ms. Ishiko Yamada, responsible for the chaos, and fired atomic breath at them, leaving their fates unknown as the portals closed.
{{Clear}}
====''[[Godzilla: Rage Across Time]]''====
[[File:GRAT_Godzilla_remastered_infobox_image.jpeg|thumb|right|200px|Godzilla fighting [[Yamata no Orochi]] in [[Godzilla: Rage Across Time issue 1|''Godzilla: Rage Across Time'' #1]]]]
{{Main|Godzilla (Godzilla: Rage Across Time)}}
In [[Israel]] during the [[Cretaceous]], Godzilla and his ally [[Anguirus]] did battle with [[Varan]] and [[Baragon]] as a stray blast of his atomic breath knocked [[Rodan]] out of the sky. Godzilla threw Varan to the ground as he then focused on Baragon who blasted Godzilla with his magma heat ray. A meteor storm caused by the arrival of the [[Xilien]]s then took place as Baragon was taken out of the fight by a meteor and Varan re-joined the battle by slamming Godzilla's head against the ground only to be beaten by an attack from Anguirus. The Xilien pawn [[Monster X|Keizer Ghidorah]] arrived on the scene and dispatched [[Mothra]] and [[Battra]], who had been battling nearby, before focusing on Godzilla and Anguirus. Keizer Ghidorah transformed into Monster X and threw Anguirus into a lava pit, enraging Godzilla into battle as the two wrestled next to the lava pit. Godzilla initially had the upper hand but was thrown into the lava by Monster X who dodged a desperate blast of atomic breath and transformed back into Keizer Ghidorah, flying away as Godzilla sunk into the lava. With Keizer Ghidorah victorious, the Xiliens placed two ''Homo erectus'' on [[Earth]] so that they could come back later to harvest Earth's resources. However, just as the Xiliens left, Godzilla re-emerged from the lava and vaporized both ''Homo erectus'' as well as a nearby ''[[Velociraptor]]'', leaving confusing fossil evidence behind in the modern age.

In Ancient [[Greece]], Godzilla appeared during a battle between two human factions at sea and destroyed both of them, with Hermes informing the other gods of this news. [[Poseidon]] investigated the story to please Aphrodite and faced Godzilla in battle at sea though was ultimately defeated by the beast, who continued travelling to Mount Olympus while swimming in a tidal wave. Godzilla arrived at Mount Olympus and was met with a bolt of lightning from [[Zeus]] as [[Ares]] also attempted to battle Godzilla but was disintegrated by a blast of his atomic breath. Zeus summoned the [[Hydra]] to fight Godzilla but Godzilla managed to kill this opponent too by pushing him into Mount Olympus, causing the entire mountain to collapse as all the gods except Zeus perished. Zeus furiously battled Godzilla and managed to finally defeat him at the cost of his divinity. Many years later in [[79]], Godzilla killed the powerless Zeus by causing the eruption of Mount Vesuvius.

In the Alps in [[218 BC]], Godzilla attacked an army led by Hannibal as he travelled and roared in the presence of [[Rome|Roman]] soldiers. Hannibal, who had survived the initial attack, vowed to defeat Godzilla by replicating the tactics of siafu ants and he leapt onto Godzilla's tail the next day and attempted to stab the monster with his sword but it shattered on impact. Godzilla unleashed his wrath upon the army led by Hannibal and killed many of them, with Godzilla later intervening in a battle between Roman soldiers and Hannibal's men by destroying the Roman soldiers as Hannibal and his men found refuge in a ravine where they plotted a plan to defeat Godzilla. The group managed to create a massive explosion using a combination of vinegar, dead bodies covered in tar and flaming arrows, burying Godzilla beneath the rubble as Hannibal and his army escaped. Godzilla, however, survived and escaped the rubble to presumably attack [[Rome]] himself.

In [[Japan]] in [[1274]], Godzilla was inadvertently awakened by Gorou Suda and Akio when they used [[Shobijin]]-enhanced arrows in an attempt to control [[Yamata no Orochi]] so that the dragon could battle the invading Mongols and their pawns [[Gigan]] and [[Megalon]]. The two brought Yamata no Orochi under control just as Godzilla blasted him with atomic breath and swiftly defeated him in combat, forcing the pair to change their plan to angering Godzilla into following them and being lured to the site where Gigan and Megalon were rampaging. They successfully did so as Godzilla entered the battle with a blast of atomic breath and began to face the two in battle, using physical attacks until he began to struggle against the pair's teamwork. Thankfully, Akio destroyed the relic being used to control the two monsters and Godzilla took advantage of their resulting confusion to send them into retreat and destroy the Mongol forces. Godzilla returned to the sea as Gorou and Akio prayed his wrath did not turn in their direction.

In [[2016]], archaeologists [[Benjamin Thompson]] and [[Nikki Kasumi]] investigated each of these sites to investigate the theory that Godzilla influenced human history prior to the modern age.
